Data Lead - Financial Services &nbsp;

Location: Warsaw, Poland | Practice Area: Data &amp; Analytics | Type: Permanent &nbsp;

Lead data transformation. Modernise data platforms. Deliver meaningful change for leading financial institutions. &nbsp;

The Role &nbsp;

At Capco, we partner with leading banks and financial institutions to deliver complex business and technology transformations, helping our clients modernise their data capabilities and drive meaningful business outcomes. &nbsp;

We are looking for an experienced Data Lead to join our Data &amp; Analytics practice in Warsaw. &nbsp;

In this role, you will lead data transformation, migration and modernisation initiatives for financial services clients, combining a solid understanding of modern data technologies with consulting, project delivery and stakeholder management capabilities. &nbsp;

You will work directly with clients to understand their business and technology challenges, shape data solutions and oversee delivery across complex transformation programmes. From defining data migration strategies and modernising data platforms to coordinating technical teams and managing senior stakeholders, you will play a key role in delivering successful outcomes. &nbsp;

We particularly welcome professionals who have delivered data initiatives for banking and financial services clients, whether their experience comes from consulting firms, financial institutions or technology delivery environments. &nbsp;

What You’ll Do &nbsp;

• Lead end-to-end data transformation, migration and modernisation initiatives for banking and financial services clients, including legacy platform migrations, cloud adoption and data platform transformation. &nbsp;

• Act as a key client-facing contact, working closely with business and technology stakeholders to define data strategies, solution approaches, technical requirements and delivery roadmaps. &nbsp;

• Shape and oversee modern data architectures, including data warehouses, data lakes, lakehouses, ETL/ELT pipelines, data integration and cloud-based data platforms. &nbsp;

• Coordinate data engineers, architects and cross-functional delivery teams, providing technical direction, managing dependencies and ensuring solutions meet business, quality and performance expectations. &nbsp;

• Support clients in improving data governance, data quality, data lineage and data management capabilities, ensuring data solutions are scalable, secure and aligned with financial services requirements. &nbsp;

What We’re Looking For &nbsp;

• Proven experience delivering complex data transformation, data migration or data platform modernisation projects for clients within banking or financial services. &nbsp;

• Solid technical understanding of modern data ecosystems, including SQL, Python, ETL/ELT processes, data pipelines, data warehousing, data integration and cloud data architectures. &nbsp;

• Experience working with modern data platforms and technologies, such as Snowflake, Databricks, Apache Spark, Airflow, dbt or equivalent solutions, with the ability to evaluate technical approaches and guide delivery teams. &nbsp;

• Demonstrated experience leading data projects or technical workstreams, coordinating data engineering teams, managing delivery risks and overseeing solution implementation. &nbsp;

• Excellent client-facing, consulting and stakeholder management capabilities, with the ability to translate complex technical concepts into business value and engage effectively with senior stakeholders. &nbsp;

